<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bagrat III of Georgia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 960–1014</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bagrat III of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagrationi-dynasty">Bagrationi dynasty</a> was the first king of a united <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. Heir through his mother to the Kingdom of Abkhazia and adopted by his kinsman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david-iii-kuropalates">David III of Tao</a>, he became King of Abkhazia in 978 and inherited the lands of the Iberian Bagratids on his father's death in 1008. In 1010 he annexed Kakheti and Hereti, bringing most Georgian lands under one crown. He died in 1014.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bagrat-iii-of-georgia.jpg" alt="Bagrat III of Georgia" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagrat_III_of_Georgia_(Bedia_mural).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
